IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tel-types`
IMPORT `tel-dates`

-- Telecommunications Act 2001 — GOALS 1 AND 2: COPPER WITHDRAWAL, DISPUTES
-- AND PERIODS.
--
--   "May Chorus stop supplying this copper service; may this party appeal a
--    determination and by when; and when do the code and review periods
--    end?"
--
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/act_public_2001_103.txt — ss 69AC-69AE,
-- 239, 241-246, Schedule 2A.

§ `Goal 1 — copper withdrawal`

-- Schedule 2A cl 1 "(3) The minimum requirements that the code must include
-- are that, before Chorus is permitted to stop supplying a copper service
-- ...,— (a) the end-user ... must be able to— (i) access a fibre service; and
-- (ii) have a connection to the fibre service installed— (A) within a
-- reasonable time frame; and (B) ... at no cost to the end-user; and (b)
-- Chorus must give the end-user, the access seeker, and the relevant fibre
-- service provider reasonable notice ...; and (c) the functionality ... must,
-- apart from legacy services, be available ... over a fibre service; and (d)
-- Chorus must provide the end-user with information about— (i) the withdrawal
-- ...; and (ii) the need to make alternative arrangements, such as battery
-- backup ...; and ... (f) if an anchor service is declared ..., the anchor
-- service ... must be available ...; and (g) a Commission 111 contact code
-- must be in force". (e) is "if reasonably practicable"; (h) prescribed
-- matters.
@ref Schedule 2A cl 1(3)
GIVEN c IS A `Copper service`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Schedule 2A protections are met for` c IF
        c's `the end-user can access a fibre service`
    AND c's `fibre installed in reasonable time at no cost`
    AND c's `reasonable notice given to end-user, access seeker and fibre provider`
    AND c's `the functionality is available over fibre`
    AND c's `withdrawal and power-failure information given`
    AND c's `any anchor service is available`
    AND c's `a Commission 111 contact code is in force`

-- s 69AC "(2) Chorus may stop supplying the service ... only if— (a) a copper
-- withdrawal code has been approved and Chorus complies with the requirements
-- of the code in relation to stopping the supply of the service; or (b) the
-- end-user chooses to have the service disconnected (other than a temporary
-- disconnection)." s 69AD(2) is the same. Compliance with the code is read as
-- including the Schedule 2A minimum protections the code must contain (fork
-- F1).
@ref ss 69AC(2), 69AD(2); Schedule 2A cl 1(3)
@export Whether Chorus may stop supplying a copper service under ss 69AC-69AD of the Telecommunications Act 2001 (NZ): only if the end-user chose permanent disconnection, or a copper withdrawal code is approved and Chorus complies with it — including the Schedule 2A protections (fibre available and installed in reasonable time at no cost, reasonable notice, the same functionality over fibre, information about withdrawal and power failures, any anchor service, and a 111 contact code in force). DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN c IS A `Copper service`  @desc Whether the section applies, the code's approval and compliance, the end-user's choice, and each Schedule 2A protection
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Chorus may stop supplying the copper service` c MEANS
    IF   NOT c's `section 69AC or 69AD applies`
    THEN `ss 69AC and 69AD do not govern this service`
    ELSE     c's `the end-user chose permanent disconnection`
         OR  (    c's `a copper withdrawal code is approved`
              AND c's `Chorus complies with the code for this service`
              AND `the Schedule 2A protections are met for` c)

-- Where neither section applies, the Act gives no answer here (changed after
-- the independent pass, which expected a refusal rather than a yes).
`ss 69AC and 69AD do not govern this service` MEANS
    REFUSE "ss 69AC and 69AD apply only to the copper services they describe"


§ `Goal 2 — disputes and periods`

-- s 242 "(2) The determination is binding on each party to the dispute who is
-- a scheme member ..., and the scheme member has no right of appeal against
-- the determination. (3) The determination is binding on each party ... who
-- is not a scheme member, except if one of those parties lodges an appeal
-- ...". s 243 "(1) A consumer or any other party to the dispute who is not a
-- scheme member may, within the time allowed under section 244(1), appeal".
-- s 244 "(1)(a) an appeal must be brought within 5 working days after the
-- determination appealed against is notified to the party ..., or any further
-- time the court allows".
@ref ss 242-244
@export Whether a party may appeal a telecommunications dispute determination to the District Court under ss 242-244 of the Telecommunications Act 2001 (NZ): only a party who is not a scheme member, within 5 working days after the determination is notified to them, or any further time the court allows. DRAFT, not reviewed by a New Zealand lawyer.
GIVEN p IS A `Dispute party`  @desc Scheme membership, the notification and appeal dates, and any further time allowed
      days IS A LIST OF DATE  @desc The Matariki Observance Days and local anniversary days
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the party may appeal the determination` p days IF
        NOT p's `a scheme member`
    AND (   p's `appeal lodged on` AT MOST `the` 5 `th working day after` (p's `determination notified on`) `, Matariki days` days
         OR (CONSIDER p's `further time allowed by the court until`
             WHEN JUST until THEN p's `appeal lodged on` AT MOST until
             WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE))

-- s 239 "(3) A person is entitled to make submissions to the Commission not
-- later than 30 working days after the date on which public notice of the
-- draft code is given." Schedule 2A cl 2 "(2) A person is entitled to make
-- submissions ... before the date that is 30 working days after the date on
-- which public notice of the draft code is given (the due date)." Hence the
-- 30th working day for a Commission code, and the calendar day before it for
-- the copper withdrawal code (fork F2).
@ref s 239(3); Schedule 2A cl 2(2)
GIVEN notice IS A DATE, copper IS A BOOLEAN
      days IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for submissions on a draft code noticed on` notice `, the copper withdrawal code` copper `, non-working days` days MEANS
    IF   copper
    THEN `the day` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (`the` 30 `th working day after` notice `, Matariki days` days)
    ELSE `the` 30 `th working day after` notice `, Matariki days` days

-- s 246 "(1) The Commission must review each industry dispute resolution
-- scheme at least once every 3 years. ... (6) ... the Commission must give
-- the following persons 20 working days to make submissions on a draft
-- report".
@ref s 246(1)
GIVEN last IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the latest day for the next scheme review after one on` last MEANS
    `add years` last 3

@ref s 246(6)
GIVEN given IS A DATE, days IS A LIST OF DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for submissions on a draft review report given on` given `, non-working days` days MEANS
    `the` 20 `th working day after` given `, Matariki days` days

-- s 69AE: "the following TSO instruments cease to apply in relation to an area
-- that becomes a specified fibre area: (a) [the local residential telephone
-- service TSO deed] (except to the extent that it relates to 111 call
-- services): (b) [the TSO network service deed]."
@ref s 69AE
GIVEN fibreArea IS A BOOLEAN, call111 IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the local residential telephone TSO still applies, specified fibre area` fibreArea `, for 111 calls` call111 IF
    (NOT fibreArea) OR call111
